# ==========================================================================
# THE WARDROBE MIRROR — Rachel catches Andrew after the first Karen loss.
#
# Fired by the `rachel-after-karen` trigger (story/graph.js): flag-set on
# read_karen_first_loss_tutorial, room-guarded to cubicle_farm, 900 ms after
# Skip's pep talk ends. Rachel is at her desk two bays over (seated, 6/10.8),
# and stays seated — a seated actor's `face` is a clamped shoulder turn,
# which is the entire beat. Pure suggestion: no flags, no gate; the mirror
# interactable in the bathroom exists whether or not this scene plays.
#
# Prose drafted claude -p --model claude-opus-4-6 (2026-08-17, two passes)
# and wired VERBATIM per HANDOFF_PACKAGE 4.5. Haruf register: she does the
# kind thing and never discusses it. The accessories-after-a-bad-meeting
# shape is played completely straight — that restraint is the reference.
# ==========================================================================
scene rachel_wardrobe
  stage concurrent
    rachel face player nowait
  Rachel: Bathroom's down the hall. Second door.
  Andrew: Sorry — what?
  Rachel: There's a mirror.
  Andrew: Do I look that bad?
  Rachel: You look like somebody who just had their first meeting.
  Rachel: I went my first week.
  Andrew: Thanks, Rachel.
  Rachel: On the left.
  stage concurrent
    rachel face rachel_monitor nowait
  Narrator: Rachel turned back to her spreadsheet. Next to her monitor was a pair of reading glasses with green frames.
  end
